{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491247-how-much-does-x-group-know","id":1491247,"title":"How much does X group know?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-24T15:13:08-07:00","id":1491247,"title":"How much does X group know?","content":"One of the things that's often taken for granted in V:TM is the fact that we, the players, know far more than many of the vampires in the setting. The question is, of course, what IS the &quot;proper&quot; amount of knowledge for your average Neonate of each sect to possess?<br /> <br /> What are the limitations for people?<br /> <br /> How much more do they know if they have an Occult score?<br /> <br /> Does it vary across Clan?<br /> <br /> How about other groups like the SAD, Inquisition, or Arcanum?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T15:50:11-07:00","id":1491254,"title":"","content":"I don't think there is a correct answer to this. It firmly goes under &quot;Ask your Storyteller&quot;. One table may play Tremere as the masters of all, others may conclude that they know vampire stuff at best, and don't even know hermetic stuff. There's been about a dozen different sidebars on this, and none of them have ever given an exact response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T15:50:33-07:00","id":1491255,"title":"","content":"My general stance used to be &quot;You know what's in the corebook&quot;, but latter editions included a lot more stuff into the corebook that I can't use that as shorthand anymore. But I generally prefer the less information the better, and the general knowledge one has of the original hardcover (2e corebook) is what I intend. (If you are playing Sabbat, then add the Lasombra and Tzimisce clan descriptions). For your own clan, you know additional clan information as provided in the original Players Guide. I don't find information in the Clanbooks to be actually needed, and the specific information in them are often contradicted by the cumulative details I have decided or been built up during earlier chronicles. That bloodlines and Independent Clans exist are known, but there is no other information available except the names of the Independents and a few sentences of description.<br /> <br /> A higher Occult score doesn't provide you anything more about vampire society in general. It's occult theory that is theoretically available to any human although few people possess Occult 4 or 5 unless they're academic scholars or practicing magicians (practicing in this case does not effective, many practicing magicians do not know any Paths of Sorcery and are just as powerless as real life occultists). In order for Occult to do anything for you, it needs to be partnered with effective knowledge (the actual Paths).<br /> <br /> As long as it is within the confines of what the corebook tells you, I allow the player to determine the specifics. While we might state in general terms that Ventrue and Toreador are likely to know more about the local vampire setting, and Gangrel and Brujah know less, so much depends on the specifics. Some sires are more informative than others. But if the character concept is one of the fringe types (Caitiff, Anarch, a Gangrel who doesn't enter urban domains and meets many other vampires) then you do know less.<br /> <br /> Knowledge of the other sect is limited to a propaganda description, although if you are better informed it may go from a two sentence description to several paragraphs.<br /> <br /> For mortal hunters, the knowledge is much less. There's basic outline that one vampire is in charge (whether she is titled Prince or Bishop), that the person is advised by a council of other powerful vampires, and that other vampires must defer to them or be destroyed. That there is a war between two groups of vampires are known. That there are multiple bloodlines of vampires descending from a founder exists, but their exact number is not known, and they know various names for each one. Most information is of a practical type - how to protect yourself from them, how you can destroy them, what works and what doesn't, how to identify them, etc. The Society of Leopold knows the most because it is institutionally the longest lasting. The Arcanum knows almost as much, but if their overall knowledge of vampires is lightly lesser than the Society of Leopold, they know a lot more about other supernatural groups and there are more active Arcanum scholars who know more local details on a specific domain. Other hunter groups know a lot less, but some of these can have greater resources (like the SAD) to run individual operations.<br /> <br /> I have prepared handouts that address this (in either actual paper form, or as a chronicle webpage) and other key chronicle subjects. It's then up to the player to decide what they know based on it. If they bring something else that was not learned in game, I veto it and tell them that is not known.<br /> <br /> I also include some information that is only real in my own chronicles, and make certain canonical information false. I let them know in advance not every bit of canon is true in my chronicles, so what they as Players know is true may not be so in the chronicle. That usually prevents them from trying to use such knowledge, since it may actually be wrong and if they're PC assumes such info, it may just make them out to be a jackass.<br /> <br /> Everything outside of that must be learned in game. I want there to be a mystery for them to learn, but have enough lore so they don't have to keep asking questions on basic things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T16:22:48-07:00","id":1491256,"title":"","content":"In another thread I suggested the average neonate with no occult score should be the following:<br /> <br /> * You know what a Prince is<br /> <br /> * You know what a Camarilla is<br /> <br /> * You know what the Anarchs are<br /> <br /> * You have heard, perhaps, the WORD Sabbat but no details other than bad vampires.<br /> <br /> * You know Seven Clans, Nine in 5th Esdition<br /> <br /> * You have heard the Warlocks may be Blood Mages.<br /> <br /> * You have heard werewolves exist but never have seen one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T16:29:53-07:00","id":1491257,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say an Occult rating would give you knowledge of the politics per se, more information on the species of creature you're dealing with. So a vampire with Occult 5 might know about Mages, even about the Euthanatos, but not about the machinations of Voormas or the inner workings of the Golden Chalice.<br /> <br /> Applying this same logic, I would say that if a PC has a reasonable expectation of having heard of or interacted with a particular group, I would have them roll Intelligence + Politics or Occult, which ever is lesser, to see if they've run across it. So, a Vampire with Politics 5 and Occult 5 has probable knowledge of the Tal Mahe Ra, but a Werewolf in Saskatchewan would automatically fail that roll, unless it was quite active in working with Wraiths for whatever reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T20:12:09-07:00","id":1491269,"title":"","content":"Nothing is true, everything is permitted. Whatever level of knowledge works best for your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T20:32:23-07:00","id":1491270,"title":"","content":"<b>The Society of Leopold</b>: Hilariously, the Society of Leopold knows everything and yet have no use for this knowledge. If you are so inclined, you can go into a secret vault which has volumes that describe vampires as the Children of Caine, 13 Clans (&quot;one of which serves the Egyptian demon Sutekh&quot;), Bloodlines, and a fair approximation of observed vampiric powers as well as probably the concept of generation. This is from countless studies, interrogations, and even the occassional repentent vampire who wishes to narc on his fellows before suicide. However, the vast-vast majority of Inquisitors DON'T CARE. Fire, stake, sunlight, how many bullets to put them down. These are the only questions you're likely to find being asked by vampire hunters. Who cares about the intricacies of demon politics? Demons! That's all!<br /> <br /> <b>NSA, SAD, and Second Inquisition</b>: In simple terms, the government refuses to believe the evidence of the supernatural and constantly demands the scientists (who are determined themselves to find alternatives) reformulate data to meet secular conclusions. They have massive amounts of data, the finest scientific minds, and many test subjects but do not believe in magic. Aliens, psychic powers, fungal infections, quantum manipulation, and even possibly ghosts but not that vampires are walking corpses animated by a divine curse. On the plus side, they have a very good idea of vampire politics and how to manipulate it as well as their resources.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcanum</b>: The Arcanum is the second most knowledgable group of supernatural among the Hunters but the problem is that if you ask an agent a question, you're likely to get three plausible answers. Vampires are the Children of Caine, vampires are the result of spirits bonded with flesh, vampires are the descendants of Risen from ancient times, the Unseelie Sidhe, and vampires are the product of immortality magics gone wrong. Oddly, their infiltration by the Order of Hermes and use of hedge magic along with other numina means that they have been exposed to more supernaturals than just vampires so they're pursuing a grand unifying theory of everything that constantly gets confronted with contradictory yet verifiable information. I mean, how likely is it that Banes, Wraiths, Changelings, Demons, Risen, Kuei-Jin, and Vampires are unrelated? That would just be silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T22:34:31-07:00","id":1491275,"title":"","content":"It depends on the type of coterie, I would say. If the characters have united out of mutual interest, they often have a higher level of shared information and notion about the supernatural. If they are a war pack designed to fight threats to vampire society their knowledge is probably more on a need-to-know basis, as their assignments will generally be given to them on a certain prey - thus they're granted specific knowledge about the specific situation. And so forth.<br /> <br /> My experience is that players rarely are all that interested in the deeper layers of the meta plot, and tend to ignore most clues they are handed. Not because they are indifferent but rather because they are often paying attention to rather mundane details.<br /> <br /> V<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;They do say, Mrs. M, that verbal insults hurt more than physical pain. They are of course wrong, as you will soon discover when I stick this toasting fork into your head.&quot;<br /> <br /> --E. Blackadder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24273-vincent","name":"Vincent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T00:35:51-07:00","id":1491279,"title":"","content":"Vampires get bored and, like how people did in medieval times, talk about what they know with their neighbours. <br /> <br /> There's no solid rule here. One city may be particularly detached from knowledge because there are few vampires and the ones who did know a lot either weren't very social or died not long after passing on the blood. Another town might be ran by a cult who wants to ensure only their version of things is known. And the last city might have everyone know everything because the elders like competing in showing off how smart they are. Even a clan that should be more consistent, like the Tremere, might not be so thorough in their education simply because the Regent doesn't think it's necessary to provide an education on X which isn't present in their city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T01:39:02-07:00","id":1491282,"title":"","content":"I tend to run it that all vampires know what's in the core book by default (with some obvious exceptions like vampires that are abandoned by their sires). Barring those exceptions, everyone knows who the Prince is as well as they're Clan primogen. Most vampires will have personally met both the Prince and Clan Primogen. If a vampire has a dot in Clan Lore or something else like that, they know most of what's in that Clan book.<br /> <br /> Past that is on a case by case basis. For example, a vampire character with a decent Mentor rating could have some scattershot supernatural info, including the occasional secret that they got from their mentor, though that info would be based around their mentors area of expertise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T12:21:07-07:00","id":1491326,"title":"","content":"Just play it by ear and be somewhat plausible with what your characters could realistically know.<br /> <br /> IE. My Brujah characters knows that his clan descends from Troile and that Carthage was very important to the clan's identity and many of the surviving meths of the clan lament it's fall and have a grudge against the Ventrue. He has some idea that Troile might have not have been the original antideuvlian and he was used as a scapegoat by the others for the troubles in the second city.<br /> <br /> He is aware of the Camarilla and the Sabbat as the big players in undead society and that there is other stranger things exist alongside humanity.<br /> <br /> In short there is no right or wrong answer to your question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T17:20:38-07:00","id":1491375,"title":"","content":"For PCs, it's mostly has to be up to the group. How do you guys want to play it. <br /> <br /> On the one hand, the PCs exist in this world and knowledge about all sorts of things might be something they'd actively seek out. I mean, I personally like some of the lore and may have read a bunch of the books. But if my life could actually depend on this information and I happened to know one or two Vampires who had lived immersed in this world for decades... well my character might reasonably know MORE than me.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, maybe you guys enjoy the idea of playing characters who don't know what's going on in the world, that's fine too. From a drama perspective, the typical &quot;origin&quot; or &quot;intro&quot; story will often follow a protagonist through this learning phase, so that makes for a fine game, too. (Though for stories, a lot of the main purpose of this is to introduce the world to the audience). A nice side effect of this is that it gives the Storyteller more freedom to completely change or facts and features of the world without having to pre-communicate this with all the players. The ability to do this and possibly even subvert expectations allows for surprise and drama. <br /> <br /> This is all a long-winded way of agreeing with the other responses and saying that you're free to play it how you want. It's even fine for different characters to have different knowledge. Just make sure you all are mostly on the same page about who knows what.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27551-manhattan-jack","name":"Manhattan Jack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T17:26:51-07:00","id":1491378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491247-how-much-does-x-group-know#post1491247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things that's often taken for granted in V:TM is the fact that we, the players, know far more than many of the vampires in the setting. The question is, of course, what IS the &amp;quot;proper&amp;quot; amount of knowledge for your average Neonate of each sect to possess?<br /> <br /> What are the limitations for people?<br /> <br /> How much more do they know if they have an Occult score?<br /> <br /> Does it vary across Clan?<br /> <br /> How about other groups like the SAD, Inquisition, or Arcanum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Im always of the position that, either groups know at least the basics that players know and then some, or not at all.<br /> <br /> I mean, all that it takes to get to know at least the basics of clan structures is one good session of torture...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T23:39:36-07:00","id":1491397,"title":"","content":"The culture of a given vampire's clan or bloodline could plausibly impact how much they know, as well. Nosferatu treat secrets as precious currency, but Brujah hold rants and raves to muster support for their causes, and Gangrel make storytelling a sacred obligation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}